From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 08:45:13 +0000
Subject: irqchip: sky1-pdc: do not read freed memory on a map error

The error path freed cd and then read cd->pdc_base for the return
value. Save the error code before the free.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
---
 drivers/irqchip/irq-sky1-pdc.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/irqchip/irq-sky1-pdc.c b/drivers/irqchip/irq-sky1-pdc.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/irqchip/irq-sky1-pdc.c
+++ b/drivers/irqchip/irq-sky1-pdc.c
@@ -221,9 +221,11 @@ static int __init sky1_acpi_pdc_irqchip_init(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	struct resource *res_dp = platform_get_resource(pdev, IORESOURCE_MEM, 0);
 	cd->pdc_base = devm_ioremap_resource(&pdev->dev, res_dp);
 	if (IS_ERR(cd->pdc_base)) {
+		int err = PTR_ERR(cd->pdc_base);
+
 		pr_err("%pACPI: unable to map pdc registers\n", pdev);
 		kfree(cd);
-		return PTR_ERR(cd->pdc_base);
+		return err;
 	}
 
 	domain = acpi_irq_create_hierarchy(0, PDC_MAX_IRQS, pdev->dev.fwnode,
-- 
Armbian

